                show pug_desc ;
            }
        
 rect 38 352 164 25

 textscale .72

 textalign ITEM_ALIGN_LEFT

 textalignx 10

 textaligny 3
}
        itemDef {
            name pug_desc
            group gamedesc
            type ITEM_TYPE_TEXTSCROLL
            text "PICKUP GAMES\nPlayers start as spectators. Open Pause > PUG Queue > Join Queue to play. The server fills the smallest teams first. Bots can hold places until a human is waiting.\n\nROUND ROTATION\nAt round end, a waiting player replaces a team's lowest scorer. Ties rotate the player who has held a spot longer. Benched players move to the back of the queue. With an empty queue, the teams stay in.\n\nINACTIVITY\nIdle players return to spectator after a warning. Waiting and watching preserve your queue position.\n\nACCOUNT POINTS\nOn an enrolled server with account scoring, signed-in players earn one point for finishing a round they started, plus one for winning."
            font 4
            visible 0
        
 rect 224 141 388 274

 textscale .88

 textalignx 7

 textaligny 9

 lineHeight 15

 forecolor .85 .92 .96 1
}

        itemDef {
            name laddermenubutton
            group game_submenu
            type ITEM_TYPE_BUTTON
            text "LADDER"
            font 2
            forecolor .76 .86 .93 1
            visible 1
            action {
                play "sound/interface/button1.wav" ;
                setitemcolor game_submenu forecolor .76 .86 .93 1 ;
                setitemcolor laddermenubutton forecolor 1 1 1 1 ;
                hide gamedesc ;
                show ladder_desc ;
            }
        
 rect 38 381 164 25

 textscale .72

 textalign ITEM_ALIGN_LEFT

 textalignx 10

 textaligny 3
}
        itemDef {
            name ladder_desc
            group gamedesc
            type ITEM_TYPE_TEXTSCROLL
            text "FIRST TO TEN\nTwo players fight for ten duel-round wins. Everyone else waits. New arrivals enter at the bottom. An asterisk means a player has yet to finish a series.\n\nMOVING UP\nThe arena rotates through neighboring ranks. The first pass pairs 1 vs 2, 3 vs 4, and so on. The next pass starts at 2 vs 3. The lower-ranked player takes the higher spot by winning.\n\nLEAVING AND RETURNING\nA disconnect cancels an unfinished series. Players below the vacated spot move up. A returning player enters at the bottom.\n\nACCOUNT POINTS\nOn an enrolled server with account scoring, signed-in players earn one point for finishing a series they started, plus one for winning. Ladder position belongs to this server session."
            font 4
            visible 0
        
 rect 224 141 388 274

 textscale .88

 textalignx 7

 textaligny 9

 lineHeight 15

 forecolor .85 .92 .96 1
}
itemDef {
			name tournament_desc
			group gamedesc
			text "BRACKET\nA random draw sets the single-elimination bracket. Byes advance unpaired entrants. Both full lineups must be connected, in the arena and ready before play starts.\n\n1v1 TOURNAMENT\nAn even field of 8 to 32 verified players enters. Play all 10 scored rounds. Each elimination wins a round. Simultaneous deaths replay the round. At 5-5, play one deciding round.\n\nTEAM TOURNAMENT\n2 to 8 teams enter at a fixed size, from 2v2 to 5v5. Players respawn. The first team to 20, 30, 40 or 50 kills respectively wins. After 10 minutes of play, the leader wins. If tied, play until one team takes the lead.\n\nRECONNECTS AND RESERVES\nA missing player pauses play. Each player has 5 minutes to reconnect in 1v1. Each team has 10 minutes to reconnect or fill the slot with a registered reserve from its own team. Repeat drops use the remaining time. Everyone readies again when the lineup is complete. Time expiry forfeits the match. If both sides expire, both are eliminated."
			type ITEM_TYPE_TEXTSCROLL
			rect 224 141 388 274
			font 4
			textscale .88
			textalignx 7
			textaligny 9
			forecolor .85 .92 .96 1
			lineHeight 15
			visible 0
		}

		

